From bb931319862e88cf62607a4385220050b6247fce Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Zac <zac@zacbowling.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Jan 2026 18:52:35 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7925/mt7921: Fix NULL pointer and mutex issues
 (18 patches)

Applied all 18 MT7925/MT7921 WiFi driver fixes:
- NULL pointer dereference fixes in vif iteration and TX path
- Missing mutex protection in reset, ROC, runtime PM, and MLO PM paths
- NULL checks in MCU STA TLV functions, link_conf, mlink
- Error handling for AMPDU, BSS info MCU commands
- Key removal fix during MLO roaming
- Lockdep assertions for mutex verification
- Firmware reload fix after failed load
- MT7921 mutex fixes (same bugs as MT7925)

These fixes prevent kernel panics and system hangs during:
- WiFi state transitions and roaming
- Suspend/resume cycles
- MLO (Multi-Link Operation) power management
- Firmware recovery

Signed-off-by: Zac Bowling <zac@zacbowling.com>
